think The crux: a per-class area sum reads WHOLE-object facts. For the CONTAINED class the whole area IS the in-rect foreground (every pixel inside); for the CLIPPED class the whole area STRICTLY EXCEEDS the in-rect foreground (some pixels outside by definition). So touched_area is only an UPPER BOUND on the true in-rect pixels -- the box-is-a-prefilter lesson lifted from the OBJECT (region_partition) to its AREA.
think Built image/region_summary.rye: RegionSummary struct (three counts, contained/clipped area, per-class holed), region_summary walking the manifest once and classifying by region_partition's exact box test, largest_contained the biggest window keep (refuses NoContained). Proved the crux on metal with a full pixel scan: contained_area 17 = A and D's in-rect foreground exactly, B's whole 8 > its 4 in-rect pixels, touched 25 > true 21, tight 34 = 34 at the no-clip fixed point.
